---
title: Herpetofauna
description: Measurement fields for specimens in a Herpetology catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 3
  badge:
    text: Beta
    variant: caution
---

Specimens in a project that uses the `Herpetology` catalog format show the
herpetofauna measurement form. Sex, life stage, and weight units work the same
way in every taxon group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

{% aside type="caution" %}

Herpetology support is in beta. Check exports against your collection's
requirements before relying on them.

{% /aside %}

## Measurements

- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage vocabulary.
- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `SVL (cm)`: snout-vent length.
- `Remarks`: additional information about the specimen.

## Parts and parasites

Herpetofauna catalogs show parasite-detection fields and the parasite tab. See
[Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/).
